**Gödel was a Platonist:**
- He believed mathematical truths exist **independently** of human minds
- He believed logic was **discovered**, not invented
- He saw his theorems as revealing the **limits of formalization**, not the limits of logic

### 7.2 What His Work Actually Shows

**His work implies:**
- Logic is a formal system
- All formal systems are incomplete
- Therefore, logic is incomplete
- Therefore, logic is a **tool**, not a **universal**

### 7.3 Why This Was Revolutionary

**Before Gödel:**
> "Logic is the universal language of truth."

**After Gödel:**
> "Logic is one language among many, and all languages are incomplete."

**Implicit Revolution:**
> "Logic is invented, not discovered—and that's okay."

